-- title:
--   Nodes of the rigid model descended to K_ℓ^G
-- statement:
--   The data are: a prime $q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; a finite set $W$ of places of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ generated over the residue field of $A$ by the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j$ in $q^{M'}$ (a place being a proper valuation subring containing the base field whose ideals are principal); a hypothesis `hle` that the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the level-$M'$ full modular function field is contained in that of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ with $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$; a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from the former field onto the above function field, i.e. a valuation subring of it whose residue map onto that field is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with degrees and orders along places; a chosen $s\in W$; a subfield $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$; a natural number $\ell$ and elements $\zeta_0,\varpi_t\in k_0$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ cut out by $A$ and an element $\varpi_b\in A_b$; a prime $\ell'$ and $\xi\in k_0$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0$ in $k_0((q))$, an algebra over $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$) compatibly with $k_0$; a nonzero $j_\ell\in K_\ell$; $\varpi_t'\in A_0$; an ideal $y$ of the chart algebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t\subseteq K_\ell$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ containing $B_t$; natural numbers $n,m$; $\gamma_0\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$; a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$; an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal; the hypothesis that the $q$-expansion of $j$ in $q^{q\ell'}$ lies in $K_\ell$; $a_0\in A_0$; a finite set $\mathit{ends}$ of subrings of $K_\ell$; and a term $\mathcal F$ of `RigidDescentHyps` for exactly these data, which is the bundle of hypotheses on them. Furthermore $G$ is a subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ assumed to be generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$, that is: for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ giving a nonzero series, every $x\in K_\ell$ whose Laurent expansion is the quotient of those series, and every ring homomorphism $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, one has $\iota_*(\tau x)\cdot q\text{-}\exp\bigl(g\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}\bigr)=q\text{-}\exp\bigl(f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}\bigr)$. Finally $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$, $B_0$ is the subalgebra of $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$, and $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ consisting of the elements lying in $W_t$. The conclusion is that the predicate `RigidDescentNodesConclusion` holds for all these data together with $G$, $K_0$, $B_0$ and $W_0'$, the package of assertions describing the nodes of the model descended to the fixed field $K_0$.
--
--   This is the descent step in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve at a supersingular point: the node data obtained on the rigid level field $K_\ell$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ are transported to the subfield fixed by the $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms, together with the corresponding chart and exceptional valuation ring. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart), on the way to the description of the reduction of $X_H$ needed for level lowering.
